      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxygen concentration of about 2 at.% is an applicable doping level.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxygen-doped alloy can be prepared by arc melting and casting.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical performance can be evaluated by room-temperature tensile testing.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen doping promotes the formation of ordered oxygen complexes in the alloy matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ordered oxygen complexes alter dislocation arrangements.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ordered oxygen complexes impede or mediate dislocation motion in a manner that enhances strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced strain hardening caused by oxygen complexes increases ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced strain hardening caused by oxygen complexes increases toughness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The approximately 2 at.% oxygen-doped alloy can exhibit about 20% elongation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen doping significantly improves elongation relative to the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxygen doping improves toughness relative to the undoped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxygen-doped alloy has a lower yield strength than the corresponding nitrogen-doped alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7299626::rubric_card::000::06c4d095e9"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
